envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-system-template-schema-hook
type: schema
id: hook
context: >-
  idearium/spec-engine/templates/system/schemas — the system template's own schemas; a new system copies them
  into its schemas/ folder and owns them from then on.
intent: >-
  James, 2026-10-05: "each component only needs to connect to the registry." · "each component has to have at least one capability, with at least one command, and events, each a node each." · "Maybe add, if applicant, data dir with the directory for the data, consumers, intent, data type/system like node, vector, database or table" · "maybe create a template or schema from that."
summary: "an end point of a component"
system: template
tags: [system-template]
source: idearium/spec-engine/templates/system
payload:
  status: REAL
  fields:
    type:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: "always \"hook\""
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: ""
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: ""
    component:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: ""
    direction:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: "in | out"
    kind:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: "http | event | direct"
    contract:
      type: object
      required: false
      description: "THE_CONTRACT_JOINS_THEM (genesis 1.6.0, applied 2026-11-23, EMB8; James: \"yes like constraints, need to be acknowledged also. my framework does all of this. at every level across any domain\"). The same block on every level (system, module, component, hook): { signature: the values it accepts, examples: ['call(args) == expected'], constraints: [{ says, kind: invariant | boundary | rule | resource, checked_by }] }. An invariant is the shape that cannot change; its depends_on are read from the wires. A hook with a contract is a piece a small model can fill; without one, it is the next thing to map."
